<title>POLAND: Polish wheat/barley prices down, rye up last week.</title>
<headline>Polish wheat/barley prices down, rye up last week.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish Agriculture Ministry said in a statement wheat and barley prices fell while rye prices rose during last week's grain auctions.</p>
<p>POLISH FARM AUCTION PRICES (AVERAGE)</p>
<p>  Product   week to Jan 25    previous week</p>
<p>   Wheat	58.46 zl/q	 59.37 zl/q</p>
<p>   Rye	  42.58 zl/q	 42.51 zl/q</p>
<p>   Barley     50.64 zl/q	 51.35 zl/q</p>
<p>NOTE - zl/q = zlotys per quintal.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom+48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
